From 86c04405f88ef2f892142d1c12c2e97939bc92cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Deng, Bing" <bing.deng@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:15:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix early loop exit and a distance-threshold typo

Major bug fixes:
1. Drop a stray break in the first-frame IMU initialization block
   (both the kf_input and kf_output paths) that broke out of the
   outer while loop right after the first sample, silently
   skipping the rest of the IMU messages already queued for that
   lidar scan window.
2. Fix Preprocess's constructor setting disA twice in a row
   instead of setting disB on the second line, so disB never got
   its intended 0.1 value.
3. Guard plane_judge against dividing by a zero-area
   cross-product and against reading two elements before the
   sorted distance array when it can't have that many, check
   mkdir()'s return value for the log directory, and wrap main()
   in a try/catch so a startup exception is logged instead of
   crashing the node.

Signed-off-by: Deng, Bing <bing.deng@intel.com>
